IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `qlt-core`
IMPORT `qlt-seat`

-- Land Tax Act 2010 (Qld) -- worked cases for the individual land owner.
--
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited texts (act-2010-015.txt, sl-2021-0019.txt,
-- act-2001-072.txt) before the encoding was run; none was copied from the encoding's output. The arithmetic is shown in
-- the comment above each case. The seat's questions are asserted directly; the regulative rules of qlt-core.l4 are
-- asserted with EVALTRACE where the trace ends FULFILLED, and #TRACEd with an "-- expect:" line where it ends in a breach
-- or with something still owed (the stable l4 cannot compare those with EQUALS). Clocks: days after the event the rule
-- names (day 0).
--
-- People and places are invented. Valuations, the averaging factor and the interest rate are illustrative inputs.

§ `Cases -- the individual land owner`

§§ `Fixtures`

-- A home owner who has lived in the home, and nowhere else, for years.
`a long-time resident` MEANS
    `my home use facts` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE

-- Moved in on 1 May; at midnight on 30 June, 2 months in, it is the principal place of residence.
`a recent arrival` MEANS
    `my home use facts` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE

-- Lives elsewhere and does not use the land as a home at all (an investor, or a co-owner who lives elsewhere).
`not living there` MEANS
    `my home use facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- Mrs Nguyen moved into residential aged care on 1 March; she lived in her Toowong house alone for 30 years before.
-- At 30 June, 4 months have passed since her last 6 months there ended. The house earned nothing.
`in aged care, house empty` MEANS
    `my home use facts` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 4 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE

-- The same, but the house was let all year at a market rent that is more than the rates and upkeep.
`in aged care, house let all year` MEANS
    `my home use facts` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 4 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE

-- The same, but let for only 5 months of the year.
`in aged care, house let 5 months` MEANS
    `my home use facts` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 4 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE

-- The same, let all year, but the rent only covers the council rates and upkeep.
`in aged care, rent covers costs` MEANS
    `my home use facts` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 4 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE

-- In care for 7 years: 84 months since the last 6 months at home, more than the 72 of s 37(6).
`in aged care for 7 years` MEANS
    `my home use facts` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 84 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- Moved out on 1 April so the house could be gutted and renovated; back by Christmas.
`renovating` MEANS
    `my home use facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE

-- Renovating, but has decided not to move back.
`renovating, not moving back` MEANS
    `my home use facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE

-- Other uses: lettings, allowable?, at most half?, family?, works from home?, ordinary work?, anything else?
`no other use`                     MEANS `my other use facts` 0 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`one boarder`                      MEANS `my other use facts` 1 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a niece and a boarder`            MEANS `my other use facts` 2 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`two boarders, no family`          MEANS `my other use facts` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a niece and a boarder, over half` MEANS `my other use facts` 2 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`one tenant with over half`        MEANS `my other use facts` 1 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`one tenant above market rent`     MEANS `my other use facts` 1 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`office work from home`            MEANS `my other use facts` 0 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
`manufacturing in the shed`        MEANS `my other use facts` 0 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`a hair salon in two rooms`        MEANS `my other use facts` 0 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE

§§ `s 7 -- when the liability arises`

-- s 7: the liability for 2026-27 arises at midnight on 30 June 2026.
#ASSERT `When does my land tax liability arise` 2026 EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2026

§§ `ss 8, 10, 11, 13, 14 -- who is the owner`

-- s 11(1)(a): a seller stays the owner until the buyer is in possession; s 11(1)(b), (2): a buyer in possession is the
-- owner even before completion.
#ASSERT `Am I the owner of this land for land tax` `the seller under an agreement for sale, the buyer not yet in possession`
#ASSERT (NOT (`Am I the owner of this land for land tax` `the seller under an agreement for sale, the buyer in possession`))
#ASSERT `Am I the owner of this land for land tax` `the buyer under an agreement for sale, in possession`
#ASSERT (NOT (`Am I the owner of this land for land tax` `the buyer under an agreement for sale, not yet in possession`))
-- s 14: the life tenant is the owner; the remainderman is not. s 13: a mortgagee in possession is not.
#ASSERT `Am I the owner of this land for land tax` `entitled to a life estate in possession`
#ASSERT (NOT (`Am I the owner of this land for land tax` `entitled to the fee simple in reversion or remainder after a life estate`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Am I the owner of this land for land tax` `a mortgagee, whether or not in possession`))
-- s 8: the owner of taxable land is liable; the owner of exempt land is not.
#ASSERT `the person is liable to pay land tax on the land (s 8)` `entitled to a freehold estate in the land, alone or with others, and in possession` TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`the person is liable to pay land tax on the land (s 8)` `entitled to a freehold estate in the land, alone or with others, and in possession` FALSE))

§§ `s 9 -- taxable land`

#ASSERT `Is this land taxable land` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is this land taxable land` TRUE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is this land taxable land` TRUE FALSE FALSE))

§§ `ss 16 to 18 -- taxable value`

-- Values $900,000, $800,000, $700,000: averaged value (900 + 800 + 700) / 3 = $800,000; the lesser is $800,000.
#ASSERT `What is the taxable value of this land` 900000 TRUE 800000 700000 1 EQUALS 800000
-- A falling value: $600,000 this year, $800,000 and $700,000 before: average $700,000; the lesser is this year's $600,000.
#ASSERT `What is the taxable value of this land` 600000 TRUE 800000 700000 1 EQUALS 600000
-- No earlier valuations (a new lot): $900,000 x an illustrative factor 0.90 = $810,000; the lesser is $810,000.
#ASSERT `What is the taxable value of this land` 900000 FALSE 0 0 0.9 EQUALS 810000
-- A factor above 1 (900,000 x 1.05 = 945,000) leaves this year's value, the lesser: $900,000.
#ASSERT `What is the taxable value of this land` 900000 FALSE 0 0 1.05 EQUALS 900000

§§ `ss 19, 22 -- aggregation and co-owners`

-- s 22(2): 2 joint tenants hold equal interests: 50%. A tenant in common holds their stated share.
#ASSERT `What share of this land am I taken to own, as a percentage` TRUE 2 0 EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `What share of this land am I taken to own, as a percentage` FALSE 3 25 EQUALS 25
-- s 19 example: 2 properties of $500,000 each are assessed together on $1,000,000.
#ASSERT `the total taxable value (s 19)` (LIST (`Holding` WITH `taxable value of the parcel` IS 500000, `the owner's share, as a fraction` IS 1, `the exempt fraction of that share` IS 0), (`Holding` WITH `taxable value of the parcel` IS 500000, `the owner's share, as a fraction` IS 1, `the exempt fraction of that share` IS 0)) EQUALS 1000000
-- ... and pay $4,500 on it, though each alone ($500,000 < $600,000) would pay nothing. Asserted (finding 4).
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I owe` 1000000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I owe land tax, in dollars, of` 4500
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I owe` 500000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I owe no land tax: my total taxable value is under the threshold`
-- An exempt home drops out: a wholly exempt $900,000 home plus $750,000 of investment land is $750,000.
#ASSERT `What is the total taxable value of my taxable land` 900000 100 100 750000 EQUALS 750000
-- Mr Lee co-owns half his daughter's Annerley house (taxable value $1,300,000) and lives in his own exempt house. His
-- half is $650,000, none of it exempt for him (s 22(3)): 500 + 1.0c x 50,000 = $1,000. Asserted (finding 7).
#ASSERT `What is the total taxable value of my taxable land` 1300000 50 0 0 EQUALS 650000
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I owe` 650000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I owe land tax, in dollars, of` 1000

§§ `s 32, Schedule 1 -- the individual rate`

-- Below $600,000: nil. At $600,000: $500 at once (finding 3).
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I owe` 599999 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I owe no land tax: my total taxable value is under the threshold`
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I owe` 600000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I owe land tax, in dollars, of` 500
-- $750,000: 500 + 1.0c x 150,000 = 500 + 1,500 = $2,000.
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I owe` 750000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I owe land tax, in dollars, of` 2000
-- $1,200,000: 4,500 + 1.65c x 200,000 = 4,500 + 3,300 = $7,800.
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I owe` 1200000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I owe land tax, in dollars, of` 7800
-- $3,500,000: 37,500 + 1.25c x 500,000 = 37,500 + 6,250 = $43,750.
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I owe` 3500000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I owe land tax, in dollars, of` 43750
-- $6,000,000: 62,500 + 1.75c x 1,000,000 = 62,500 + 17,500 = $80,000.
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I owe` 6000000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I owe land tax, in dollars, of` 80000
-- $12,000,000: 150,000 + 2.25c x 2,000,000 = 150,000 + 45,000 = $195,000.
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I owe` 12000000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I owe land tax, in dollars, of` 195000
-- The bands join: at $3,000,000 the $1m band gives 4,500 + 1.65c x 2,000,000 = 37,500, the next band's base.
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I owe` 3000000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I owe land tax, in dollars, of` 37500
-- "for each $1 more than": $1,000,001 is $1 more: 4,500 + 1.65c = $4,500.0165; 50 cents more counts nothing.
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I owe` 1000001 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I owe land tax, in dollars, of` 4500.0165
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I owe` 1000000.5 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I owe land tax, in dollars, of` 4500
-- Trustees and companies are not covered.
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I owe` 750000 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not covered: land owned as a trustee or through a company (s 32(1)(b), Schedule 2, s 33)`

§§ `s 32(1)(c), Schedule 3 -- the absentee rate`

-- Below $350,000: nil under both parts.
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I owe` 349999 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `I owe no land tax: my total taxable value is under the threshold`
-- $350,000: general $1,450; surcharge 3.0c x (350,000 - 349,999 = 1) = 3 cents: $1,450.03 (finding 5).
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I owe` 350000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `I owe land tax, in dollars, of` 1450.03
-- $750,000: general 1,450 + 1.7c x 400,000 = 8,250; surcharge 3.0c x 400,001 = 12,000.03; total $20,250.03.
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I owe` 750000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `I owe land tax, in dollars, of` 20250.03
-- $2,500,000: general 33,750 + 1.5c x 250,000 = 37,500; surcharge 3.0c x 2,150,001 = 64,500.03; total $102,000.03.
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I owe` 2500000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `I owe land tax, in dollars, of` 102000.03
-- $12,000,000: general 175,000 + 2.5c x 2,000,000 = 225,000; surcharge 3.0c x 11,650,001 = 349,500.03; $574,500.03.
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I owe` 12000000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `I owe land tax, in dollars, of` 574500.03
-- On $750,000 an absentee pays 20,250.03 - 2,000 = $18,250.03 more than a resident individual.
#ASSERT `How much more land tax would I pay as an absentee` 750000 EQUALS 18250.03
-- On $500,000 a resident pays nothing; an absentee pays 1,450 + 1.7c x 150,000 + 3.0c x 150,001 = 1,450 + 2,550 + 4,500.03.
#ASSERT `How much more land tax would I pay as an absentee` 500000 EQUALS 8500.03

§§ `s 31 -- absentee`

-- An Australian citizen living in London is never an absentee (s 31(3)(c)).
#ASSERT `Am I an absentee` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not an absentee: an Australian citizen (s 31(3)(c))`
-- A British national without a permanent visa who lives in London is an absentee (s 31(1)).
#ASSERT `Am I an absentee` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `an absentee: does not ordinarily reside in Australia (s 31(1))`
-- A permanent visa holder is not, wherever they live (s 31(3)(d)).
#ASSERT `Am I an absentee` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not an absentee: the holder of a permanent visa (s 31(3)(d))`
-- A New Zealand citizen on a special category visa who lives in Auckland: no s 31(3) exception, so an absentee (finding 6).
#ASSERT `Am I an absentee` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `an absentee: does not ordinarily reside in Australia (s 31(1))`
-- A temporary visa holder who lives in Brisbane but was overseas on 30 June: an absentee unless they satisfy the
-- Commissioner they ordinarily reside in Australia (s 31(2)).
#ASSERT `Am I an absentee` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `an absentee, unless the Commissioner is satisfied the person ordinarily resides in Australia (s 31(2))`
-- The same person at home on 30 June and in Australia most of the year: not an absentee.
#ASSERT `Am I an absentee` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not an absentee: ordinarily resides in Australia`
-- Posted to Singapore by a Brisbane employer for 3 years: not an absentee, if the Commissioner is satisfied (s 31(3)(b)).
#ASSERT `Am I an absentee` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not an absentee, if the Commissioner is satisfied the absence is on the employer's duty and will not be longer than 5 years (s 31(3)(b))`
-- After 6 years away the exception stops (s 31(4)), and they no longer ordinarily reside here: an absentee.
#ASSERT `Am I an absentee` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `an absentee: does not ordinarily reside in Australia (s 31(1))`
-- A State public officer away on duty is not an absentee (s 31(3)(a)).
#ASSERT `Am I an absentee` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not an absentee: a public officer absent on duty (s 31(3)(a))`

§§ `ss 36 to 38 -- used as a home`

#ASSERT `the use of the land as a home (ss 36 to 38)` `a long-time resident` EQUALS `used as the home: the 6 month residency test (s 36(1)(a))`
-- 2 months in: only s 36(1)(c), on the Commissioner's satisfaction.
#ASSERT `the use of the land as a home (ss 36 to 38)` `a recent arrival` EQUALS `used as the home, if the Commissioner is satisfied it is the owner's principal place of residence (s 36(1)(c))`
#ASSERT `the use of the land as a home (ss 36 to 38)` `not living there` EQUALS `not used as the home (s 36)`
-- s 37: in care, house empty: taken to be her home.
#ASSERT `the use of the land as a home (ss 36 to 38)` `in aged care, house empty` EQUALS `taken to be used as the home: the owner receives care (s 37)`
-- s 37(4): let all year at a market rent above costs: not her home (finding 8).
#ASSERT `the use of the land as a home (ss 36 to 38)` `in aged care, house let all year` EQUALS `not used as the home (s 36)`
-- s 37(5)(a): let for 5 months: still her home. s 37(5)(b): rent only covering rates and upkeep: still her home.
#ASSERT `the use of the land as a home (ss 36 to 38)` `in aged care, house let 5 months` EQUALS `taken to be used as the home: the owner receives care (s 37)`
#ASSERT `the use of the land as a home (ss 36 to 38)` `in aged care, rent covers costs` EQUALS `taken to be used as the home: the owner receives care (s 37)`
-- s 37(6): after 6 years (here 84 months) it stops.
#ASSERT `the use of the land as a home (ss 36 to 38)` `in aged care for 7 years` EQUALS `not used as the home (s 36)`
-- s 38: renovating, intending to return: the home, if the Commissioner is satisfied of s 38(a).
#ASSERT `the use of the land as a home (ss 36 to 38)` `renovating` EQUALS `taken to be used as the home, if the Commissioner is satisfied the owner is temporarily living elsewhere because of the demolition or renovation (s 38)`
#ASSERT `the use of the land as a home (ss 36 to 38)` `renovating, not moving back` EQUALS `not used as the home (s 36)`
-- The seat question gives the same answer from plain inputs.
#ASSERT `Is my land used as my home` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 4 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `taken to be used as the home: the owner receives care (s 37)`

§§ `s 36(2) -- the principal place of residence factors`

-- 2 months there, family there, belongings in, roll still at the old address, services on, bought to live in: 5 factors.
#ASSERT count (`Which factors point to this being my principal place of residence` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `Which factors point to this being my principal place of residence` 2 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST "s 36(2)(a): has occupied a residence on the land for 2 months"
#ASSERT `Which factors point to this being my principal place of residence` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS EMPTY

§§ `ss 39, 40 -- renting out a room, working from home, other uses`

#ASSERT `the non-exempt purpose question (ss 39, 40)` `no other use` EQUALS `no non-exempt purpose: the land is used for nothing but the home (s 39(2)(a))`
-- 1 boarder at market rent in under half the floor area: an allowable letting (s 40(3)(a)).
#ASSERT `the non-exempt purpose question (ss 39, 40)` `one boarder` EQUALS `no non-exempt purpose: only allowable lettings or working from home, so the Commissioner may not decide one (s 40)`
-- 2 lettings, one to a niece, together under half: permitted (s 40(3)(b)).
#ASSERT `the non-exempt purpose question (ss 39, 40)` `a niece and a boarder` EQUALS `no non-exempt purpose: only allowable lettings or working from home, so the Commissioner may not decide one (s 40)`
-- 2 lettings with no family letting, or together over half, or 1 over half, or 1 above market rent: not permitted.
#ASSERT `the non-exempt purpose question (ss 39, 40)` `two boarders, no family` EQUALS `a non-exempt purpose, if the Commissioner is satisfied the other use is substantial (s 39(2))`
#ASSERT `the non-exempt purpose question (ss 39, 40)` `a niece and a boarder, over half` EQUALS `a non-exempt purpose, if the Commissioner is satisfied the other use is substantial (s 39(2))`
#ASSERT `the non-exempt purpose question (ss 39, 40)` `one tenant with over half` EQUALS `a non-exempt purpose, if the Commissioner is satisfied the other use is substantial (s 39(2))`
#ASSERT `the non-exempt purpose question (ss 39, 40)` `one tenant above market rent` EQUALS `a non-exempt purpose, if the Commissioner is satisfied the other use is substantial (s 39(2))`
-- An employee's office work in a home study is not excluded work (s 40(5) example); manufacturing in a shed is.
#ASSERT `the non-exempt purpose question (ss 39, 40)` `office work from home` EQUALS `no non-exempt purpose: only allowable lettings or working from home, so the Commissioner may not decide one (s 40)`
#ASSERT `the non-exempt purpose question (ss 39, 40)` `manufacturing in the shed` EQUALS `a non-exempt purpose, if the Commissioner is satisfied the other use is substantial (s 39(2))`
#ASSERT `the non-exempt purpose question (ss 39, 40)` `a hair salon in two rooms` EQUALS `a non-exempt purpose, if the Commissioner is satisfied the other use is substantial (s 39(2))`
-- The seat question: 3 boarders is never a permitted number.
#ASSERT `Can my home be treated as used for a non-exempt purpose` 3 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a non-exempt purpose, if the Commissioner is satisfied the other use is substantial (s 39(2))`

§§ `s 39(3) -- the substantial use factors`

-- A salon in 2 rooms with an employed stylist, $45,000 gross last year: (b), (c) and (d).
#ASSERT count (`Which factors point to the other use being substantial` FALSE TRUE TRUE 45000) EQUALS 3
-- Exactly $30,000 is not "more than $30,000": (d) is not listed (no amount is prescribed by the Regulation).
#ASSERT `Which factors point to the other use being substantial` FALSE FALSE FALSE 30000 EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `Which factors point to the other use being substantial` FALSE FALSE FALSE 30001 EQUALS LIST "s 39(3)(d): last year's gross income from the land was more than $30,000"

§§ `ss 22(3), 41, 42 -- is my home exempt?`

#ASSERT `the home exemption (ss 22(3), 41, 42)` FALSE FALSE FALSE `a long-time resident` `no other use` EQUALS `wholly exempt as the owner's home (s 41)` `no further condition`
#ASSERT `the home exemption (ss 22(3), 41, 42)` FALSE FALSE FALSE `a long-time resident` `one boarder` EQUALS `wholly exempt as the owner's home (s 41)` `no further condition`
#ASSERT `the home exemption (ss 22(3), 41, 42)` FALSE FALSE FALSE `a long-time resident` `a hair salon in two rooms` EQUALS `wholly exempt as the owner's home (s 41), unless the Commissioner decides the other use is substantial: then only the part used as the home is exempt (ss 39, 42)` `no further condition`
#ASSERT `the home exemption (ss 22(3), 41, 42)` FALSE FALSE FALSE `a recent arrival` `no other use` EQUALS `wholly exempt as the owner's home (s 41)` `if the Commissioner is satisfied the land is the owner's principal place of residence (s 36(1)(c))`
#ASSERT `the home exemption (ss 22(3), 41, 42)` FALSE FALSE FALSE `renovating` `no other use` EQUALS `wholly exempt as the owner's home (s 41)` `if the Commissioner is satisfied the owner is temporarily living elsewhere because of the demolition or renovation (s 38(a))`
#ASSERT `the home exemption (ss 22(3), 41, 42)` FALSE FALSE FALSE `not living there` `no other use` EQUALS `not exempt: the land is not used as the owner's home (s 36)`
-- Mr Lee's half of his daughter's house: no benefit (s 22(3)). So too a spouse co-owner who lives elsewhere (finding 7).
#ASSERT `the home exemption (ss 22(3), 41, 42)` FALSE FALSE TRUE `not living there` `no other use` EQUALS `not exempt for this co-owner, who does not use the land as their home (s 22(3))`
-- The daughter, the co-owner who lives there, has her half wholly exempt.
#ASSERT `the home exemption (ss 22(3), 41, 42)` FALSE FALSE TRUE `a long-time resident` `no other use` EQUALS `wholly exempt as the owner's home (s 41)` `no further condition`
#ASSERT `the home exemption (ss 22(3), 41, 42)` TRUE FALSE FALSE `a long-time resident` `no other use` EQUALS `not covered: land owned as a trustee, by a company or by a time-sharing manager`
#ASSERT `the home exemption (ss 22(3), 41, 42)` FALSE TRUE FALSE `a long-time resident` `no other use` EQUALS `not covered: a home on more than one parcel`
-- The seat question from plain inputs: a long-time resident working from home in a study.
#ASSERT `Is my home exempt` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `wholly exempt as the owner's home (s 41)` `no further condition`

§§ `ss 42A, 42B -- moving house`

-- Tom bought in Paddington in February 2026 and moved in; his Ashgrove house, his home at 30 June 2025, is sold and
-- settled in August 2026. For 2026-27 the Ashgrove house is exempt under s 42A.
#ASSERT `Is my old home exempt while I move` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the old home is exempt for the current financial year, to the extent it was exempt at the previous liability date (s 42A(2))`
-- He let Ashgrove after moving out: s 42A(3)(b).
#ASSERT `Is my old home exempt while I move` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not exempt under s 42A: rents or profits were received (s 42A(3))`
-- He will not have sold it by 30 June 2027: s 42A(1)(b)(iii) fails.
#ASSERT `Is my old home exempt while I move` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not exempt under s 42A: the conditions of s 42A(1) are not met`
-- Paddington came with a tenant who left within 6 months: the rent before moving in does not count (s 42A(4)).
#ASSERT `Is my old home exempt while I move` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the old home is exempt for the current financial year, to the extent it was exempt at the previous liability date (s 42A(2))`
#ASSERT `Is my old home exempt while I move` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not exempt under s 42A: rents or profits were received (s 42A(3))`
-- s 42B: the new home bought before 30 June, moved into after; the present home sold by the next 30 June.
#ASSERT `Is my new home exempt before I move` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the new home is exempt for the current financial year, to the extent the current home is exempt at this liability date (s 42B(2))`
-- The present home is the home only because of a renovation (s 38): s 42B(1)(a)(i) excludes it.
#ASSERT `Is my new home exempt before I move` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not exempt under s 42B: the conditions of s 42B(1) are not met`
#ASSERT `Is my new home exempt before I move` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not exempt under s 42B: rents or profits were received (s 42B(3))`

§§ `s 44A -- telling the Commissioner after a move`

-- Still owning the old home at 30 June 2027: notice within 28 days, by 28 July 2027.
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Commissioner about my move` `s 44A(1)(a): the person still owns the old home at the next liability date` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2027) EQUALS `yes: I must give the Commissioner notice no later than` (DATE_FROM_DMY 28 7 2027)
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Commissioner about my move` `none: the move went as assessed` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2027) EQUALS `no: this section does not require me to give notice`
-- s 44A(4): "The person must give notice": the party is the person.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 44A -- after a moving exemption, the person must tell the Commissioner within 28 days of a relevant matter` `s 44A(1)(a): the person still owns the old home at the next liability date`) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the person` `give notice of the details of the relevant matter` 28)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 44A -- after a moving exemption, the person must tell the Commissioner within 28 days of a relevant matter` `none: the move went as assessed`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 60)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the person, "s 44A(4), (5): ..." (notice on day 29)
#TRACE (`s 44A -- after a moving exemption, the person must tell the Commissioner within 28 days of a relevant matter` `s 44A(1)(b): rents or profits were received in the way s 42A(3) describes`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the person` DOES `give notice of the details of the relevant matter` AT 29

§§ `s 44 -- telling the Commissioner after a renovation`

-- Assessed for 2026-27 under s 38; not back by 30 June 2027: notice by 28 July 2027.
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Commissioner I have not moved back` TRUE FALSE 2027 EQUALS `yes: I must give the Commissioner notice no later than` (DATE_FROM_DMY 28 7 2027)
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Commissioner I have not moved back` TRUE TRUE 2027 EQUALS `no: this section does not require me to give notice`
-- s 44(2): "The person must give notice": the party is the person.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 44 -- after a renovation exemption, the person must tell the Commissioner within 28 days if they have not moved back` TRUE FALSE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the person` `give notice that the land is not being used as the principal place of residence` 28)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the person, "s 44(2), (3): ..." (notice on day 29)
#TRACE (`s 44 -- after a renovation exemption, the person must tell the Commissioner within 28 days if they have not moved back` TRUE FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the person` DOES `give notice that the land is not being used as the principal place of residence` AT 29

§§ `s 53, Regulation s 2 -- farm land`

#ASSERT `Is my farm land exempt` `all of the land is used solely for the business of primary production` `maintaining animals to sell them or their bodily produce, including natural increase (r 2(a))` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `exempt: land used for primary production by an individual (s 53)`
#ASSERT `Is my farm land exempt` `part of the land is used solely for the business of primary production` `propagating or cultivating plants or mushrooms to sell them or their produce, in soil, containers or hydroponically (r 2(c))` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the part used for primary production is exempt; the Commissioner apportions the taxable value (s 53(3))`
-- An absentee farmer, owning as an individual, gets no s 53 exemption (s 53(2)(a)) (finding 11).
#ASSERT `Is my farm land exempt` `all of the land is used solely for the business of primary production` `other agriculture, dairy farming or pasturage (r 2(e))` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not exempt: an absentee individual owner (s 53(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Is my farm land exempt` `all of the land is used solely for the business of primary production` `none of these activities` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not exempt: the activity is not one prescribed by Regulation s 2`
#ASSERT `Is my farm land exempt` `none of the land is used solely for the business of primary production` `cultivating land to sell produce (r 2(b))` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not exempt: the land is not used solely for a business of primary production`
-- The trustee of a family trust whose beneficiaries are all resident individuals, cropping the whole farm: (a) excludes
-- a trustee, but (b) exempts the land if all the beneficiaries are (a), (c) or (d) persons. (b) is not encoded: not
-- covered, not "not exempt" (finding 21).
#ASSERT `Is my farm land exempt` `all of the land is used solely for the business of primary production` `cultivating land to sell produce (r 2(b))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: land owned as a trustee or by a company, which may be exempt under s 53(2)(b) or (c)`
-- A trustee who is also an absentee: under (b) the beneficiaries decide, not the trustee's own residence: not covered.
#ASSERT `Is my farm land exempt` `all of the land is used solely for the business of primary production` `cultivating land to sell produce (r 2(b))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not covered: land owned as a trustee or by a company, which may be exempt under s 53(2)(b) or (c)`
-- Land owned through a company, part grazed: (c) a relevant proprietary company, not encoded: not covered.
#ASSERT `Is my farm land exempt` `part of the land is used solely for the business of primary production` `maintaining animals to sell them or their bodily produce, including natural increase (r 2(a))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: land owned as a trustee or by a company, which may be exempt under s 53(2)(b) or (c)`
-- A trustee's land not used for primary production at all: s 53(1) does not apply, whoever owns it.
#ASSERT `Is my farm land exempt` `none of the land is used solely for the business of primary production` `cultivating land to sell produce (r 2(b))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not exempt: the land is not used solely for a business of primary production`

§§ `s 23 -- a deceased person's land`

#ASSERT `Who is taken to own the deceased person's land` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the deceased person, until the administration of the estate is complete (s 23(4))`
#ASSERT `Who is taken to own the deceased person's land` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `each relevant beneficiary, for their interest, if the Commissioner is satisfied s 23 applies (s 23(3))`
#ASSERT `Who is taken to own the deceased person's land` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 23 does not apply: the estate administrator does not own the land in that capacity at the liability date, or the administration is complete`
-- Death on 15 March 2026: the next 30 June is 30 June 2026. On 30 June 2026: that day (s 23(6)). On 1 July 2026: 30 June 2027.
#ASSERT `Up to which 30 June can the deceased person's land stay exempt` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2026) EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2026
#ASSERT `Up to which 30 June can the deceased person's land stay exempt` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2026) EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2026
#ASSERT `Up to which 30 June can the deceased person's land stay exempt` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2026) EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2027
-- The home, exempt at 30 June 2025, left empty since a death in March 2026; the executor holds it at 30 June 2026,
-- the administration is not complete and no s 23(2) request was made: the deceased person is taken to own it (s 23(4))
-- and it is exempt at 30 June 2026 (s 23(5)). Kept in the same use: exempt. Let from May: not exempt.
#ASSERT `Is the deceased person's land exempt at the first 30 June after the death` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE `not used since the death` EQUALS `exempt at the next 30 June after the death: land taken to be owned by the deceased person (s 23(4)(a), (5))`
#ASSERT `Is the deceased person's land exempt at the first 30 June after the death` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE `used since the death only for the purpose it was used for at the last 30 June before the death` EQUALS `exempt at the next 30 June after the death: land taken to be owned by the deceased person (s 23(4)(a), (5))`
#ASSERT `Is the deceased person's land exempt at the first 30 June after the death` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE `used since the death for another purpose` EQUALS `not exempt under s 23(5): not exempt at the last 30 June before the death, or used since the death for another purpose`
#ASSERT `Is the deceased person's land exempt at the first 30 June after the death` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `not used since the death` EQUALS `not exempt under s 23(5): not exempt at the last 30 June before the death, or used since the death for another purpose`
-- The executor asked for the beneficiaries to be assessed (s 23(2)): if the Commissioner is satisfied, they are the
-- owners (s 23(3)), s 23(4) does not apply "to the extent subsection (3)" does, and s 23(5) has no land to exempt
-- (finding 22).
#ASSERT `Is the deceased person's land exempt at the first 30 June after the death` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `not used since the death` EQUALS `s 23(5) does not apply: on the request, the beneficiaries are taken to own the land (s 23(3)), if the Commissioner is satisfied s 23 applies`
-- The administration was complete by 30 June 2026: s 23(4) ends "until the administration of the estate is complete".
#ASSERT `Is the deceased person's land exempt at the first 30 June after the death` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `not used since the death` EQUALS `s 23(5) does not apply: the deceased person is not taken to own the land (s 23(1), (4))`
-- The land is no longer held as executor at 30 June 2026 (for example, already transferred): s 23(1) does not apply.
#ASSERT `Is the deceased person's land exempt at the first 30 June after the death` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `not used since the death` EQUALS `s 23(5) does not apply: the deceased person is not taken to own the land (s 23(1), (4))`

§§ `s 34 -- working abroad longer than 5 years`

-- Away since 3 March 2021; 5 years reached on 3 March 2026: notice by 31 March 2026.
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Commissioner that my absence has passed 5 years` TRUE TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 3 3 2026) EQUALS `yes: I must give the Commissioner notice no later than` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 2026)
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Commissioner that my absence has passed 5 years` TRUE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 3 3 2026) EQUALS `no: this section does not require me to give notice`
-- s 34(2): "The taxpayer must ... give notice": the party is the taxpayer.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 34 -- a taxpayer working abroad must tell the Commissioner within 28 days after 5 years of absence` TRUE TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the taxpayer` `give notice that the absence from Australia has passed 5 years` 20)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 34 -- a taxpayer working abroad must tell the Commissioner within 28 days after 5 years of absence` TRUE FALSE) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 60)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the taxpayer, "s 34(2): ..." (notice on day 29)
#TRACE (`s 34 -- a taxpayer working abroad must tell the Commissioner within 28 days after 5 years of absence` TRUE TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the taxpayer` DOES `give notice that the absence from Australia has passed 5 years` AT 29

§§ `s 76 -- applying for the exemption`

-- Exempt last year, same owner, same reason: no application needed (s 76(2)).
